<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Feodor III of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1661–1682</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Fyodor III Alekseyevich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Feodor III was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from 1676 to 1682, the eldest surviving son of Alexis. Educated by the scholar Simeon Polotsky and often ill, he ruled through favourites who carried out reforms, most notably the abolition in 1682 of mestnichestvo, the system that ranked nobles for office by the service record of their ancestors. His early death without a son led to the joint reign of his brothers Ivan V and Peter I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/feodor-iii-of-russia.jpg" alt="Feodor III of Russia" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Feodor_III_of_Russia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
